hooks=[('Recognition → unexpected real version','A familiar game mechanic happens in a physical setting.','Show the game and its physical counterpart immediately; establish one changed rule; deliver a small result before widening the challenge.','11–18, 89–90','q8QnRcTleS0'),('Forced choice','Viewers choose before the creator does.','Put both options on screen; allow a short guess window; reveal the consequence and use it to create the next decision.','12, 16–17, 46, 73, 76','UR45HsG-mY8'),('First meeting / missing person','A known voice gains a real face and a new relationship.','Use one familiar cue, show the meeting, then turn it into a shared task rather than an extended greeting.','2, 5–7, 49','a6a1GihedNA'),('Visible consequence','The game action changes something real.','Show the consequence prop in frame before the attempt; trigger it immediately after a loss; keep a score so each round changes the situation.','21–29, 44, 55','pRIHc5C4Q_A'),('Contrast you can test','Two options invite a verdict the viewer can check.','Use the same task, framing and judging criteria on both sides; reveal actual costs after an initial guess.','30, 36, 64, 67, 69, 97','T2MSUmQmiWU'),('Transformation with a deadline','A visible starting problem must become a finished result.','Show the before state and recipient need; identify a deadline; reveal meaningful progress instead of a shopping montage.','14, 40–41, 52, 60','9IT6t8Pzk7w'),('Social disagreement','Two people interpret the same evidence differently.','Start with conflicting answers; let each give one concise reason; resolve with an observable answer or let the unresolved judgment become the point.','4, 8–10, 42, 50–51, 78','aaf3Q1mqxdg'),('Uncertainty in a bounded location','A clear objective is interrupted by a specific unknown.','Show the environment before the scare, establish the task and rules, then preserve enough quiet for a real change to register.','39, 81–86, 89','5hwV95hXSN4')]
creative='<section id="creative" class="chapter"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / Keep a live question</span><h2>Creative</h2></div><p>Practical hook types and ways to carry the episode.</p></div><p>These are proposed IRL adaptations of visible niche formats and the intelligence system. Their effectiveness needs an episode test; the measured moment evidence is in Post-Production.</p><div class="two-grid">'
for name,why,how,ids,ref in hooks:creative+=f'<article class="text-card"><h3>{name}</h3><p><b>Audience question:</b> {why}</p><p>{how}</p><p class="fine">Ideas {ids} · <a href="{E[ref]["url"]}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Niche reference: {H(E[ref]["title"])}</a></p></article>'
creative+='''</div><h3>Three ways to structure a full episode</h3><div class="three-grid"><article class="text-card"><h4>Rounds with consequences</h4><p>For quizzes, food and crew games: promise → simple first round → harder choice → changed score → final contest. Each result changes the next attempt. Keep one score graphic and remove repeated rules.</p></article><article class="text-card"><h4>A task in the real world</h4><p>For builds, shifts and travel: visible goal → first attempt → real obstacle → revised approach → finished result. Cut transport that changes nothing; keep a person correcting Niz or a decision that changes the route.</p></article><article class="text-card"><h4>Access through a relationship</h4><p>For family and meetups: recognition → shared task → disagreement or surprise → a revealing story → something they accomplish together. A guest introduction earns its length through action.</p></article></div><div class="callout"><b>First-frame contract:</b> The pictured people, object or dilemma should be visible immediately. By 15 seconds the rule and stakes should be clear; by 30 seconds a real attempt should be underway. These are writing targets, not measured universal retention thresholds.</div><h3>Re-hook after each payoff</h3><p>Show what changed, then open the next specific question. Use a harder round, a shrinking budget, a newly revealed clue or a guest taking control. Avoid a new promise that the episode never answers, long resets after a win, and repeated shouting that adds no information.</p></section>'''

creative=creative.replace('</section>',solo_creative+'</section>')

