post=f'''<section id="post-production" class="chapter"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">05 / Edit from the measured moments</span><h2>Post-Production</h2></div><p>MoreNizarisaqt retention curves and timestamped decisions.</p></div><p>The source catalogue contains 475 retention curves. This explorer selects 28 relevant videos with annotated moments: guessing games, horror, night shifts, progression and survival. Dashboard pull: September 5, 2026; data through September 3. <a href="../channels/UCvEtdkmA1aR9Tt7iXIiQXbw.html">Open the channel analysis →</a></p><div class="retention-lab"><label for="retention-select">Compare a video</label><select id="retention-select">{''.join(f'<option value="{v["videoId"]}">{H(v["title"])}</option>' for v in D['retention']['cases'])}</select><div id="retention-stats" class="metrics"></div><svg id="retention-chart" viewBox="0 0 1000 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="chart-title chart-desc"><title id="chart-title">Audience retention</title><desc id="chart-desc">Measured watch ratio across video duration. Use the moment buttons below to inspect peaks and drops.</desc></svg><div class="chart-controls"><label>Inspect time<input id="retention-time" type="range" min="0" value="0" step="1"></label><output id="retention-readout" aria-live="polite"></output><a id="retention-watch" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch this timestamp ↗</a><a id="retention-source" href="#">Full source analysis →</a></div><p class="fine">The curve plots the source watch ratio, which can exceed 100% when sections are replayed. Times and 5s/15s/30s values interpolate the available percentage-duration samples; they are not second-by-second event measurements. Green markers are source-tagged peaks; coral markers are source-tagged drops. A tagged drop may still outperform the usual drop at that position.</p><div id="moment-list"></div></div>
 <h3>What to carry into an IRL edit</h3><div class="two-grid"><article class="text-card"><h4>Show the solution, then advance</h4><p>Singer Tower at 6:20 records a sustained rise through five samples (+0.9% of viewers present in the source annotation). Keep the solved state legible. At 6:51, the post-verdict aside has a 2.3× normal stop rate. Test a shorter bridge into the next question.</p><a href="../channels/UCvEtdkmA1aR9Tt7iXIiQXbw/pDlG2tmh0LY.html">Source and caveats →</a></article><article class="text-card"><h4>Keep a strong reaction connected to an outcome</h4><p>The 6:45 Adele verdict in the same video shows a one-sample +5.6% rise among viewers present. At 3:53, a scream transition has a 2.6× normal stop rate. The practical test is a clear verdict followed by the next choice, with reaction length earned by the result.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pDlG2tmh0LY&t=405s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review the 6:45 moment →</a></article><article class="text-card"><h4>Distinguish a reveal from the reset after it</h4><p>Mining Factory marks the unlock at 6:49 as a peak and the following 6:56 segment as a drop. Preserve the reward and inspect the transition into another purchase or grind. For a real build, reveal the working upgrade before moving on.</p><a href="../channels/UCvEtdkmA1aR9Tt7iXIiQXbw/olRuWh8AFWM.html">Inspect both moments →</a></article><article class="text-card"><h4>Review interruptions and repeated effort</h4><p>Grow a Chicken Fighter flags 7:41 around a subscribe/like aside. Drain Water flags a shop/menu moment at 10:29 and a grind admission at 15:55. Trial cuts should retain the relevant decision while shortening repeated explanation.</p><a href="../channels/UCvEtdkmA1aR9Tt7iXIiQXbw/ceLlgiGLyYw.html">Review the source →</a></article></div>
 <h3>Moment patterns across the channel</h3><p>The source grouped 119 usable moments from 36 of 40 recent analyzed videos. <b>No category had a consistent effect.</b> The adjusted percentage-point values below compare flagged moments with the typical flagged moment of the same kind and video position; they are not a promised lift in overall retention.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Tagged moment type</th><th>Adjusted median effect</th><th>Moments / videos</th><th>p-value</th><th>Edit implication to test</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(f'<tr><th scope="row">{a}</th><td>{b}</td><td>{c}</td><td>{d}</td><td>{e}</td></tr>' for a,b,c,d,e in [('Viewers scrub back','+1.9 pp','26 / 16','.152','Keep the payoff legible; a replay can also signal confusion.'),('Scripted / NPC dialogue','+1.3 pp','13 / 9','.267','Keep dialogue that changes a choice; trim repetitive exposition.'),('Reveal / pull / unlock','+0.8 pp','10 / 8','1.000','Preserve the reveal and shorten the reset afterward.'),('Explaining plan / setup','+0.4 pp','8 / 8','1.000','Show the rule while action begins.'),('Tangent / aside','0.0 pp','19 / 12','1.000','Judge the specific aside; the category alone gives no answer.'),('Shop / menu','−0.2 pp','12 / 10','.774','Keep the purchase decision, compress navigation.'),('Combat / boss','−0.4 pp','13 / 10','.774','Clarify the objective and what each attempt changes.'),('Grind / rebirth admission','−1.9 pp','6 / 6','1.000','Replace repeated effort with progress and a fresh target.'),('Mistake / failure','−2.4 pp','12 / 11','.774','Keep consequences; avoid repeating an unchanged failure.')])+'''</tbody></table></div><p class="fine">Groups are observational and small. First-30-second/coarse/unusable moments were excluded by the source. These are gaming-channel patterns to test in IRL, not established IRL retention laws.</p><h3>Editor handoff</h3><ol><li>Mark the promised payoff and the next unanswered question in every scene.</li><li>Review 15 seconds on each side of a flagged moment; distinguish confusing action, a rewind, an ad break and a spent payoff.</li><li>Make one specific proposed change, keep the original cut, and record what would support or disprove it.</li><li>After release, compare early retention and relative performance at matched video positions; do not attribute a whole-video result to one cut.</li></ol></section>'''

