shortsection+='''</div><h3>Four-week test, attached to real shoots</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>Production plan</th><th>What to compare</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>1</th><td>Film 2 self-contained Shorts on a local crew-game day.</td><td>A question-first opening versus an action-first opening on comparable rounds.</td></tr><tr><th>2</th><td>Make 2 food or physical-game Shorts while filming the related episode.</td><td>Clear real-world payoff versus a game-to-real-life match cut.</td></tr><tr><th>3</th><td>Repeat the more promising format with a different specific prompt.</td><td>Whether the result repeats without increasing spend.</td></tr><tr><th>4</th><td>Keep the best repeatable format and produce 2 new examples.</td><td>Viewed versus swiped, engaged views, average percentage viewed, subscribers and related-video traffic.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Each Short should make sense without the full episode. Use a related-video link when the long video delivers the same promise; avoid withholding the Short’s entire answer just to force a click. Raw Short views and long-form views are different measures.</p><details><summary>Full 96-Short source sample</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Creator</th><th>Short</th><th>Rounded lifetime views</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(f'<tr><td>{H(s["channel"])}</td><td><a href="{s["url"]}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{H(s["title"])}</a></td><td>{fmt(s["views_rounded"])}</td></tr>' for s in D['shorts']['sample'])+'</tbody></table></div></details></section>'

